{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HAB",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will stand upon my watch, and seat myself upon the tower, and will watch to see what he will say to me, and what I shall answer when I am reproved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD answered me, and said, Write the vision, and make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " plain upon tables, that he may run that readeth it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the vision ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it may tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, his soul ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is lifted up, is not upright in him: but the just shall live by his faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes also, because he transgresseth by wine, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a proud man, neither keepeth at home, who enlargeth his desire, as hell, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as death, and cannot be satisfied, but gathereth to him all nations, and collecteth to him all people:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall not all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, Woe to him that increaseth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not his! how long? and to him that ladeth himself with thick clay!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall they not rise suddenly that shall bite thee, and awake that shall disturb thee, and thou shalt be for booties to them?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because thou hast laid waste many nations, all the remnant of the people shall lay thee waste; because of men's blood, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to him that coveteth an evil covetousness to his house, that he may set his nest on high, that he may be delivered from the power of evil!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast consulted shame to thy house by cutting off many people, and hast sinned ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the stone shall cry out of the wall, and the beam out of the timber shall answer it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to him that buildeth a town with blood, and establisheth a city by iniquity!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not from the LORD of hosts that the people shall labor in the very fire, and the people shall weary themselves for very vanity?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the earth shall be filled with the knowledge of the glory of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to him that giveth his neighbor drink, that puttest thy bottle to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and makest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " drunken also, that thou mayest look on their nakedness!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art filled with shame for glory: drink thou also, and let thy foreskin be uncovered: the cup of the LORD'S right hand shall be turned to thee, and shameful vomiting ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on thy glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the violence of Lebanon shall cover thee, and the spoil of beasts, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made them afraid, because of men's blood, and for the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What profiteth the graven image that its maker hath graven it; the molten image, and a teacher of lies, that the maker of his work trusteth therein, to make dumb idols?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to him that saith to the wood, Awake; to the dumb stone, Arise, it shall teach! Behold, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " laid over with gold and silver, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no breath at all in the midst of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAB.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HAB.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his holy temple: let all the earth keep silence before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
